 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# Lateral sources not included when qualifying columns\n\n## Description\n\nWhen using lateral joins in SQL queries, columns from lateral sources are not properly qualified. This happens in the `_get_all_source_columns` method in the `Resolver` class, which only processes columns from `selected_sources` but ignores `lateral_sources`.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a query with a lateral join:\n\n```sql\nSELECT u.user_id, l.log_date \nFROM users AS u \nCROSS JOIN LATERAL (\n  SELECT l1.log_date \n  FROM (\n    SELECT l.log_date \n    FROM logs AS l \n    WHERE l.user_id = u.user_id AND l.log_date <= 100 \n    ORDER BY l.log_date LIMIT 1\n  ) AS l1\n) AS l\n```\n\n2. Try to qualify columns in this query\n\nExpected: All columns should be properly qualified, including those from lateral sources.\nActual: Columns from lateral sources are not properly qualified, which can lead to incorrect query transformations or errors.\n\nThis issue affects any SQL query that uses lateral joins, as the columns from lateral sources are not being included in the source columns dictionary.\n</issue>\n",
